  "name": "C3 COMPLIMENT",
  "code": "1047",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"111\" data-end=\"269\"><strong data-start=\"111\" data-end=\"142\">C3 (Complement Component 3)</strong> is a key protein of the <strong data-start=\"167\" data-end=\"188\">complement system</strong>, which helps the immune system defend against pathogens and clear damaged cells.</p>\n<p data-start=\"271\" data-end=\"292\">This test is used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"623\">\n<li data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"386\">\n<p data-start=\"296\" data-end=\"386\">Evaluate <strong data-start=\"305\" data-end=\"331\">immune system activity</strong>, especially in <strong data-start=\"347\" data-end=\"386\">autoimmune or inflammatory diseases</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"387\" data-end=\"485\">\n<p data-start=\"389\" data-end=\"485\">Monitor <strong data-start=\"397\" data-end=\"417\">disease activity</strong> in <strong data-start=\"421\" data-end=\"459\">Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE)</strong> or <strong data-start=\"463\" data-end=\"485\">glomerulonephritis</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"486\" data-end=\"567\">\n<p data-start=\"488\" data-end=\"567\">Help diagnose <strong data-start=\"502\" data-end=\"527\">complement deficiency</strong>, which can lead to recurrent infections</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"568\" data-end=\"623\">\n<p data-start=\"570\" data-end=\"623\">Assess <strong data-start=\"577\" data-end=\"605\">immune complex disorders</strong> or <strong data-start=\"609\" data-end=\"623\">vasculitis</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong data-start=\"609\" data-end=\"623\">Decreased C3 &ndash; Clinical Implications</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE)</strong></td>\n<td>Low C3 due to consumption in immune complex-mediated inflammation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis</strong></td>\n<td>Transiently low C3 due to immune complex formation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Membranoproliferative glomerulonephritis</strong></td>\n<td>Persistently low C3 often seen in complement-mediated kidney disease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sepsis or severe infections</strong></td>\n<td>May cause complement consumption</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Congenital C3 deficiency</strong></td>\n<td>Rare; leads to recurrent pyogenic infections</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
